    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0653" n="641" xml:id="pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chinese Minister of War</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Chen Cheng</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to Lieutenant General Alvan C.
                            Gillem, Jr.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-03">April [3?] 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor to inform you that I was appointed as Acting Government
                    Representative by His Excellency the Generalissimo to the Committee of Three to
                    continue the discussion during General Chang Chi Chung’s absence.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">General Chen Cheng</hi></signed> (<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">seal</hi>)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
